Z||000000||trigger||03-05-2001||08:56 PM||||where can i find the best price for a new fuel pump for my 88 coupe. it has a four cylinder auto.  thanks for any info.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Trigger.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Archie||03-05-2001||11:12 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by trigger:<BR><B>where can i find the best price for a new fuel pump for my 88 coupe. it has a four cylinder auto.  thanks for any info.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Do yourself a big favor..... Use a Delco Pump only, no matter what the cost it is the best deal.<P>Archie<P>If it Ain't Delco, it won't go.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||V8Fiero||03-05-2001||11:39 PM||||I agree with archie. I bought one from Napa for 35 bucks. Got it put in and it didnt work at all. Talk about being P'Oed. Had to pull the tank again............. Needless to say the manager got a few choice words from me.<P>AC DELCO is my choice as well. Spend the money. Would hate for you to have to go through what I did having to pull the tank AGAIN......<P>Scott||||reg||1
