Z||000005||rockcrawl||03-06-2001||03:07 PM||||I always use Delco pumps. Autozone carries Delco fuel pumps for about $60.<P>Kyle, if your 4.5 has throttle body injection it should run fine on a 4 cyl Fiero pump. If you find it's starving for fuel, the Cadillac pump should fit with little or no modifications. If you have a port injected 4.5 (1990 only I think), you'll need a V6 Fiero pump or the Cadillac pump.<P>------------------<BR>Jon Lagler<BR>'87 GT<BR>4.9 liter V8 Testarossa Spyder (under construction)<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rockcrawlsig.jpg"> ||||reg||7
Z||000006||AL||03-06-2001||06:51 PM||||autozone sells ac delco,i put one on my indy and no problems yet,to bad you live to far my uncle is the manager and i got it for 32 bucks.<B>AL</B> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/AL_sig.gif"> <BR>86gt <BR>84indy<P>------------------<BR> ||||reg||1
